        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-2BR4MX",
      "invariant": "INV-CK3PTB",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-end-message-belongs-to-its-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Binds the move status to the identity of the shown rows through useStatusFor. A selection clears the status; an end reports no earlier/later change and preserves the selection. Shown order/view/row changes invalidate the old status; no continuation-stop message exists.",
      "role": "propagation-persistence"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "3f4f48e8b7fc8fbe3e202d423976d38219d30c6b",
        "content": "sha256:612c3cee6a94e2b191d9d42e6374fdebdfa07b595632f62d8458702779b318bb",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "useStatusFor"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-3CW82B",
      "invariant": "INV-CK3PTB",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-end-message-belongs-to-its-rows",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Stores the status together with the rows the committed tree showed when the move was made, and gives it out only while the rows it is called with are those rows. A layout effect drops the stored status in the commit that shows other rows, so it cannot return with the same rows later. Setting the same status for the same rows keeps the state object, and nothing is updated during a render.",
      "role": "primary-authority"
    },
    {
      "anchor": {
        "blob": "3f4f48e8b7fc8fbe3e202d423976d38219d30c6b",
        "content": "sha256:7130f52a0b62856ae1670706ac5dadc2579465d01cd989fd4ba70ebabdf79bff",
        "locator": {
          "kind": "symbol",
          "name": "forward"
        }
      },
      "id": "RLZ-W9PW0P",
      "invariant": "INV-MWCCQM",
      "origin": {
        "handoffEntry": "MIK-R39@v1-kept-partial-family-stop",
        "leaf": "260928-MIK-L39"
      },
      "rationale": "Chooses the next real-change row after the current position and skips the current occurrence; if none exists it returns end. Traversal selects/focuses a row, never a roster-continuation stop or automatic page read.",
      "role": "enforcement"
    },
    {
